$$\begin{aligned} \tan 71^\circ &= \dfrac{AB}{1244} \\ \therefore AB &= 1244\times\tan 71^\circ \end{aligned}$$

In $\triangle BDH$ (right-angled at $B$, $\angle BHD=78^\circ$):

\exfigure{339_q33_s3}

$$\begin{aligned} \tan 78^\circ &= \dfrac{BD}{1244} \\ \therefore BD &= 1244\tan 78^\circ \end{aligned}$$

